license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - ideology
  - social ontology
  - individuation
  - decontestation
  - historical kinds
  - emergence
abstract: "What individuates an ideology? This paper proposes a grid-relative criterion: an ideology is individuated by what it does to a grid of twenty questions it did not author and cannot abolish, operating as a bounded weighting over the cells and as a chain of six operators understood as species of decontestation. Families are treated as historical kinds; a closing protocol specifies how the signatures can be estimated and disconfirmed."
